From: shaohong.dong <shaohong.dong.cq@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] aic8800: expose experimental monitor TX build status

Expose a read-only module parameter so preflight checks inspect the loaded
driver rather than inferring raw TX support from monitor RX capability.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Q6A experimental OpenHD diagnostics]
Signed-off-by: shaohong.dong <shaohong.dong.cq@gmail.com>

--- a/usr/src/aic8800-usb-5.0+git20260123.5f7be68d-7/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
+++ b/usr/src/aic8800-usb-5.0+git20260123.5f7be68d-7/USB/driver_fw/drivers/aic8800/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_main.c
@@ -75,6 +75,15 @@
     u8_l wowlan_param1[] = {0x01,0x2a,0x06,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,
                         0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff,0xff};
 #endif
+
+/* Read-only build marker, not a claim about firmware/RF capability. */
+#ifdef CONFIG_RWNX_MON_XMIT
+static bool openhd_monitor = true;
+#else
+static bool openhd_monitor = false;
+#endif
+module_param(openhd_monitor, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(openhd_monitor, "Experimental monitor TX compiled (not RF qualified)");
 
 static char *wifi_mac_addr = 0;
 
